<title>USA: Cocensys says Novartis ends ACEA 1021 deal.</title>
<headline>Cocensys says Novartis ends ACEA 1021 deal.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>CoCensys Inc said Novartis AG decided not to participate further in the development of ACEA 1021, CoCensys' compound for the treatment of stroke and traumatic brain injury.</p>
<p>The decision was influenced by preliminary results from a recently completed Phase I safety trial, it said.</p>
<p>It said preliminary results from the most recent trial showed crystals of ACEA 1021 in the urine of some of the subjects.  This is a potentially dose-limiting effect that CoCensys will continue to evaluate, it said.</p>
</text>
